{
  "simulation_id": "eu_gdpr_implementation_10actor",
  "title": "GDPR Compliance Dilemma",
  "objective": "Simulate stakeholder negotiations around GDPR compliance tradeoffs between business viability, regulatory enforcement, technical constraints, and research impacts.",
  "brief": "EU General Data Protection Regulation rollout (2016-2018). GDPR imposed massive compliance costs on businesses worldwide, with some US sites blocking EU users entirely rather than comply. Stakeholders: a bootstrapped SaaS startup founder facing EUR 20K compliance costs that represent 15% of annual revenue, a national data protection authority enforcement officer tasked with processing thousands of complaints, an ad-tech engineer who built the tracking systems now being dismantled and faces potential job loss, and a medical researcher whose patient data sharing across hospitals got restricted by consent requirements.",
